      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c021357a58d0a7e70c3e515|full_name}: Kind of! It makes sense from some standpoint, and it's something some other games follow too for the same reason, to reduce API calls, though it's usually a much shorter 'cooldown' on other games! It's possible the 60 second rule only applys to external applications trying to use the API?\nI imagine as they grow their infrastructure for VRChat they'd consider changing it some time if it was really needed!\nI'm all for the social menu updating properly, I feel like that's more of a bug/a limiation they have right now rather than intentional. :)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
